    "title": "Air Force Veteran's Clemency in 2001 Murder Denied, Execution Scheduled For Next Month - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Nick Mordowanec ,\n10 hours ago Convicted murderer and U.S. military veteran James Pavatt will be executed next month. The Oklahoma Pardon and Parole Board denied his clemency during the Wednesday, Oct. 14, hearing, even as roughly 100 fellow veterans vouched for Pavatt's life to be spared. The death row inmate is scheduled to be executed Nov. 12, two days after his 73rd birthday. Read full article\n2",
